nd prose-section extract/inline is planned on top of [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the rename.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]prose_note_type.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/prose_note_type.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-qj[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-qj/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rename the Rust article engine to prose[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]engine-rename[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]engine-rename: move the article engine module and its Rust identifiers [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]to prose names, with byte-identical CLI, JSON, help, and docs output.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob prose with permanent legacy aliases[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]prose-cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after engine-rename[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]prose-cli: one predicate reads both type spellings, writers emit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][\\[prose]], bob prose becomes canonical with bob articles as a hidden [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]alias, copy and docs move to prose, and a section-numbers flag plus a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]host probe ship; wire vocabulary stays frozen.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bob Prose in Obsidian[/bold #D7AFFF]                                         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]prose-plugins[dim] · [dim][/dim]after prose-cli[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]prose-plugins: four plugins detect both spellings, display names and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]command titles change under unchanged ids, a Toggle section numbers [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]command lands, plugin docs are fixed, and the bundles deploy with a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]currency marker.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Host gate, vault cutover, and canonical plugin calls[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]prose-vault[dim] · [dim][/dim]after prose-cli, prose-plugins[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]prose-vault: pass the host-currency gate, retype the one live note and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rename the vault's type files, switch plugin calls to bob prose, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]apply only accepted memory decisions.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Plan prose-section extract and inline[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold white on #AF5FFF] xlarge [/bold white on #AF5FFF]\n    [#AF87FF]prose-sections[dim] · [dim][/dim]after prose-vault[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]prose-sections: author and propose the epic for bob prose extract/inline[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and its Obsidian keymap, bound by the research requirements, with the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]research's open questions embedded as decisions.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-qj","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","phase_bead_id":"bob-cli-qj.1","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-4e53ac377ee0cca13fc10b19e9aaa461","started_at":"2026-11-26T15:58:33.810130+00:00","state":"completed"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"f86d4a0b1f883804fdc9a80f67e199db3bf69c5d3aa7967ce30c5e578bf78f65","path":"agents/bbugyi200.ap